UPDATE companies SET description='Cascade Systems Technology operates from Hillsboro, Oregon, where the company says it has served as a supplier of choice for more than 36 years. The business describes itself as a electronic contract manufacturer specializing in electronic manufacturing services (EMS) for customers across the United States.

Its capabilities span the full spectrum of electronic assembly: surface-mount technology with BGA and micro-BGA placement, through-hole, press-fit, microelectronics, board de-panelization, conformal coating (acrylic, silicone, polyurethane), box-build assembly, mechanical assembly, cable and wire-harness integration, design-for-testability and design-for-manufacturing support, and rework/repair. The firm also provides system-level integration and testing services.

CST serves military and aerospace programs, medical-device OEMs, semiconductor capital-equipment makers, clean-energy and EV/battery-storage companies, sensor and instrumentation firms, and industrial-controls builders. Reference customers cited include a semiconductor manufacturer, a clean-energy/EV power-supply producer, a semiconductor fab-infrastructure supplier, and the National Defense University.

The company emphasizes its decades of hands-on experience across account management, engineering, and design as a differentiator, saying that depth helps it identify and resolve challenging manufacturing problems quickly. It also highlights its domestic U.S. footprint and certifications — ISO 9001:2015, ITAR registration, IPC-A-610F, UL ZPVI2, UL-796, ISO 14001, and ESD compliance — as core to its quality commitment.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 14001','ITAR','IPC-A-610F','UL ZPVI2','UL-796','ESD compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Surface mount technology (SMT)", "BGA and micro-BGA placement", "Through-hole assembly", "Press-fit assembly", "Microelectronics assembly", "Board de-panelization", "Conformal coating (acrylic, silicone, polyurethane)", "Box build assembly", "Mechanical assembly", "Cable and wire harness assembly", "Design for testability (DFT)", "Design for manufacturing (DFM)", "Rework and repair", "System integration", "Functional and in-circuit testing", "LED assembly", "IoT device assembly (wireless sensor networks, control systems, automation)"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defense", "Medical Devices", "Semiconductor Manufacturing", "Clean Energy & EV / Battery Storage", "Sensors & Instrumentation", "Industrial Controls", "AI / Data Center / Quantum Computing", "Energy", "Commercial Electronics"], "materials": ["Acrylic conformal coating", "Silicone conformal coating", "Polyurethane conformal coating"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 36 years as a supplier of choice", "ISO 9001:2015, ITAR, IPC-A-610F, UL ZPVI2, UL-796, ISO 14001, and ESD certifications", "Decades of hands-on experience across account management, engineering, and design", "Domestic U.S. electronic contract manufacturing in Hillsboro, Oregon", "Full-spectrum electronic assembly under one roof (SMT, microelectronics, box build, test)"], "facts_used": ["Hillsboro, Oregon location -> /", "Over 36 years as supplier of choice -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /", "ITAR registered -> /", "IPC-A-610F certified -> /", "UL ZPVI2 certified -> /", "UL-796 certified -> /", "ISO 14001 compliant -> /", "ESD compliant -> /", "Services: SMT, PCB assembly, mechanical assembly, microelectronics, conformal coating, box build, testing -> /", "Industries: aerospace, energy, medical device, semiconductor, manufacturing -> /", "Customer testimonials from semiconductor, clean energy, etc. -> /", "Blog posts about AI, UAVs, NDU, CHIPS Act -> /", "About page confirms EMS contract manufacturing in Hillsboro, Oregon -> /about", "Additional project scopes: LED, electric vehicle equipment, sensors, cables, wire assemblies, IoT -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Cascade Systems Technology is a premier electronic contract manufacturing company specializing in Electronic Manufacturing Services (EMS) in Hillsboro, Oregon.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cascade-systems-technology' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Casco Bay Molding was founded in February 2000 by Andrew Powell in Sanford, Maine, with a vision to produce silicone and thermoplastic products domestically.

The vertically integrated facility combines product development, an in-house precision machine shop, and injection molding under one roof. It specializes in high-volume silicone and thermoplastic molding, including overmolding of differing durometers, and has produced over one million menstrual cups for global B2B customers. The shop also manufactures Class I and II medical device components such as surgical handles, CPAP parts, valves, tubes, and custom gaskets, and handles FDA registration and retail packaging.

The company serves the medical device, menstrual health, respiratory equipment, energy extraction, and personal protective equipment sectors. Notable projects include the Wandah™ vaginal applicator developed with nurse practitioner Hope Jensen, the patented Flip Disc menstrual disc, and the Casco Shield™ face shield created with Thermoformers of New England during the COVID-19 pandemic.

Casco Bay Molding differentiates itself through its vertically integrated model that shortens tooling lead times via its partnership with Legu Tool & Mold, its ISO 13485:2016 certification and FDA registration for medical manufacturing, and its two-decade depth in silicone and thermoplastic processing. The firm was named Maine MEP Manufacturer of the Year in 2018.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','ISO 9001','FDA registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Silicone injection molding", "Thermoplastic injection molding", "Overmolding (multi-durometer)", "In-house precision tooling / machine shop", "Product development and design", "Medical device component design", "Mold making", "FDA product registration", "Retail packaging", "Ultrasonic welding", "Part assembly and handling", "Inspection", "Prototyping", "Patent development support", "Face shield manufacturing", "Menstrual cup manufacturing", "CPAP component manufacturing", "Scuba gear manufacturing", "Energy extraction plastic parts molding", "Antimicrobial product development (upcoming)", "Biocompatibility testing", "Material certification", "Automation integration", "Regulatory compliance consulting"], "industries": ["Medical device manufacturing (Class I and II)", "Menstrual health products", "Respiratory equipment / CPAP", "Energy extraction", "Personal protective equipment (PPE)", "Scuba / diving equipment", "Non-governmental organizations (humanitarian aid)", "Wholesale / retail packaging"], "materials": ["Medical-grade silicone", "Thermoplastic", "Polypropylene"], "equipment": ["In-house machine shop", "Automation systems (EAM, Province Automation)"], "volume": "High-volume production; over 1 million menstrual cups manufactured", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated design, tooling, and production under one roof", "In-house precision machine shop reduces mold lead time and cost", "ISO 13485:2016 certified and FDA registered for medical device manufacturing", "Over 20 years of high-volume silicone and thermoplastic injection molding experience", "Produced over one million menstrual cups for global B2B customers"], "facts_used": ["Founded February 2000 by Andrew Powell in Sanford, Maine -> /about-us", "ISO 13485:2016 certified and FDA registered -> /", "In-house precision machine shop and tooling partnership with Legu Tool & Mold -> /", "High-volume silicone and thermoplastic injection molding, overmolding capability -> /", "Manufactured over 1 million menstrual cups for global B2B customers -> /", "Medical device components: surgical handles, CPAP parts, valves, tubes, gaskets -> /", "Wandah applicator developed with Hope Jensen -> /", "Flip Disc patented menstrual disc with overmolded hinge -> /", "Casco Shield face shield produced with Thermoformers of New England -> /", "ISO 9001 certified since 2003 -> /about-us", "Maine MEP Manufacturer of the Year 2018 -> /about-us", "Automation partners EAM and Province Automation -> /about-us", "Materials: medical-grade silicone, thermoplastic, polypropylene -> /", "Ultrasonic welding, assembly, inspection capabilities -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Casco Bay Molding is a vertically integrated, FDA registered, ISO 13485:2016 Certified product development and injection molding facility located in Sanford, Maine.", "founded_year": "2000", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='casco-bay-molding' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Case Medical Inc. is based in Bloomfield, New Jersey, and was founded in 1992. The company began as a supplier of custom graphics trays to medical device manufacturers.

Today, Case Medical manufactures a range of medical instrument processing solutions. Its core products include DIN-sized SteriTite® universal sealed containers, modular MediTray® inserts, SuperNova® and NovaPlus cleaning chemistries, SteriTite® case carts, and the CaseTrak360® software platform for OEM tracking and inventory management. The company also offers an IFU scanner and consulting services such as cost-benefit analysis.

The company serves healthcare facilities, hospital sterile processing departments, operating rooms, and medical device manufacturers. Its container system is FDA-cleared for all current sterilization modalities and medical devices, and the firm emphasizes universal compatibility to reduce inventory and operating-room delays.

Case Medical differentiates itself through several factors: it is the only medical device reprocessing manufacturer recognized by the U.S. EPA as a Safer Choice Partner of the Year (2022, 2023, 2024); its products are validated by independent laboratories and universities; it offers customization of instrument sets to surgeon preferences; and it has filed a patent for Digital Visualization, integrating the SteriTite container with CaseTrak360 software for paperless counts and AI-enhanced workflow.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical instrument processing solutions", "Sterilization container manufacturing (SteriTite\u00ae)", "Modular tray system manufacturing (MediTray\u00ae)", "Cleaning chemistry formulation (SuperNova\u00ae, NovaPlus)", "Case cart manufacturing (SteriTite\u00ae Case Carts)", "Software development (CaseTrak360\u00ae OEM tracking)", "IFU scanning", "Instrument set customization", "Consulting (cost-benefit analysis)", "Education and training (Case Academy)", "Infection prevention consulting", "Sustainable product design (EPA Safer Choice)"], "industries": ["Healthcare facilities", "Hospital sterile processing departments", "Operating rooms", "Medical device manufacturers (OEM)", "Medical device reprocessing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["FDA-cleared container system for all sterilization modalities", "EPA Safer Choice Partner of the Year (2022\u20132024)", "Products validated by independent laboratories and universities", "Customizable instrument sets tailored to surgeon preferences", "Digital Visualization patent integrating SteriTite containers with CaseTrak360 software"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1992 as supplier of custom graphics trays to medical device manufacturers -> /", "Headquartered in Bloomfield, New Jersey -> db", "Manufactures SteriTite universal sealed containers and MediTray modular inserts -> /", "Offers cleaning chemistries (SuperNova, NovaPlus) -> /", "Provides CaseTrak360 OEM tracking software -> /", "FDA cleared container system for all sterilization modalities -> /", "EPA Safer Choice Partner of the Year 2022-2024 -> /", "Products validated by independent laboratories and universities -> /", "Customizable instrument sets per surgeon preferences -> /", "Digital Visualization patent filed for SteriTite and CaseTrak360 integration -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Case Medical, Inc. (\"Case Medical\") is a U.S. manufacturer of high quality, cost effective instrument processing products and services.", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='case-medical-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Clark brought over 30 years of respiratory experience and identified a service gap that larger providers could not fill. The couple founded the company with a vision of hometown care and a family atmosphere, aiming to create a business where staff and patients interact on a first-name basis.

The operation runs with a small team that includes a branch manager, delivery technician, marketing representative, and general manager, though total headcount and facility size are not disclosed.

