UPDATE companies SET description='Cedar Creek Energy is based in Blaine, Minnesota, and has been operating since 2007. The company began as an electrical and general contractor with a dedicated focus on solar development, engineering, procurement, and construction (EPC), as well as operations and maintenance.

The firm designs, installs, and operates commercial solar photovoltaic arrays across the Midwest, delivering full EPC services from initial design through final commissioning. It also integrates energy storage systems with solar arrays.

Cedar Creek Energy serves commercial and industrial property owners. A notable project includes the first approved MnPACE (Property Assessed Clean Energy) financed project in Minnesota. Its customer base spans commercial real estate, industrial facilities, and other entities seeking to reduce energy costs through solar power.

The company states that its integration of development, EPC, and O&M under one roof distinguishes it in the market. It also highlights over 16 years of experience with complex solar arrays and recognition such as MNSEIA''s 2024 Project of the Year and a 2025 Top Solar Contractor ranking by Solar Power World.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system design", "Engineering, procurement, and construction (EPC)", "Commercial solar installation", "Solar operations and maintenance (O&M)", "Energy storage system integration", "Civil and electrical construction", "On-call electrical service", "Project financing and incentive optimization", "MnPACE financing expertise"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Industrial", "Renewable energy"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Integrated development, EPC, and O&M under one roof", "Over 16 years of experience with large, complex solar arrays", "Thousands of commercial solar projects completed", "Energy storage system integration with solar arrays", "Recognized as MNSEIA 2024 Project of the Year and 2025 Top Solar Contractor"], "facts_used": ["Based in Blaine, Minnesota -> db", "Founded in 2007 -> db", "Electrical and general contractor with focus on solar development, EPC, O&M -> db", "Designs, installs, operates commercial solar PV arrays throughout Midwest -> db", "Over 16 years experience with large complex solar arrays -> db", "Thousands of solar projects completed -> db", "Integrated development, EPC, O&M under one roof -> db", "Energy storage integration -> /", "Commercial and industrial solar -> /", "First approved MnPACE financed project -> db", "MNSEIA 2024 Project of the Year -> /about-us", "2025 Top Solar Contractor by Solar Power World -> /about-us", "Voted One of Minnesota''s Best by Star Tribune -> /about-us", "Civil and electrical construction services -> db", "On-call electricians for service work -> db", "Project financing and incentive optimization -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Cedar Creek Energy is an electrical and general contractor with a specific focus on solar development, EPC services, maximizing system operation, and system maintenance.", "founded_year": "2007", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cedar-creek-energy-solar-company-minnesota' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Celestica''s Maple Grove, Minnesota site operates as a dedicated facility within the company''s global network, focusing on highly regulated aerospace, defense, and health technology markets. The location was added to Celestica''s footprint to provide a U.S.-based center of excellence for engineering, manufacturing, and after‑market services. The site''s legal entity remains AbelConn, LLC, which was rebranded to Celestica Maple Grove.

The facility combines an in‑house engineering center of excellence with on‑site manufacturing, offering services that span design engineering, prototyping, build‑to‑print production, electromechanical assembly, and obsolescence management. Core manufacturing processes include printed circuit board assembly (surface‑mount, through‑hole, hybrid), chassis and line‑replaceable unit (LRU) assembly, backplane fabrication, automated soldering, plating, conformal and parylene coating, potting, underfill, staking, and bonding. The site also provides inspection and test, product certification, and repair and overhaul services for civil aircraft. Prototypes can be delivered in four to six weeks plus material lead times.

Primary customers are commercial aerospace and defense primes requiring high‑reliability systems for aircraft, land, sea, air, and space platforms, as well as medical device companies ranging from startups to multinational brands. The site''s ITAR‑compliant volume production and NADCAP‑qualified processes support defense programs, while its ISO 13485 certification enables medical device manufacturing.

