UPDATE companies SET description='Central Coast Live Foods traces its roots to 2014 when Central Coast Juicery opened its first location in Pacific Grove, California. The juice shop was founded with a mission to bring healthy, fresh, organic juice to the local community. A team member named Max is noted handling customer communications, though the founders are not identified in public materials. The company is now headquartered in Watsonville, California.

The company manufactures Kraut Krackers, a fermented cracker made from four organic ingredients. The product is produced through a fermentation process that the company says enhances nutritional quality and nutrient absorption. After initial sales through the juice shops, demand outpaced the original production capacity, prompting a scale-up that now places the crackers in retail stores across California. Specific facility size, headcount, and annual volumes are not disclosed.

Customers cited in reviews include individuals managing gut-health conditions such as Crohn’s disease, vegans seeking clean-label snacks, and athletes looking for electrolyte-rich post-workout options. The product is marketed as soy-free, sugar-free, seed-oil-free, gluten-free, and vegan.

The shift from juice to crackers was driven by customer demand for nutrient-dense foods without ultra-processed ingredients. The company states that Kraut Krackers were the only product meeting their standards for minimal processing—just four simple ingredients—and that fermentation differentiates the snack by providing probiotics, fiber, electrolytes, and healthy fats in a shelf-stable format.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fermentation", "Clean-label food formulation", "Small-batch production", "Retail packaging", "Direct-to-consumer fulfillment"], "industries": ["Health food", "Snack food", "Organic food", "Specialty food retail", "Direct-to-consumer food"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Four-ingredient organic formulation", "Fermentation for probiotic content and nutrient bioavailability", "Free from gluten, soy, added sugar, and seed oils", "Vegan and suitable for specialty diets", "Produced and packaged in California"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2014 in Pacific Grove, CA as Central Coast Juicery -> /", "Headquarters in Watsonville, California -> db", "Manufactures Kraut Krackers fermented crackers with four organic ingredients -> /", "Fermentation process used for probiotic content and nutrient absorption -> /", "Products sold direct-to-consumer and in retail stores across California -> /", "Product claims: soy-free, sugar-free, seed oil free, gluten-free, vegan -> /", "Team member Max handles customer service -> /", "Originated from juice shop customer demand for nutrient-dense foods -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Kraut Krackers kept selling so much so that we couldn''t make them fast enough. We decided to ramp up the production and now Kraut Krackers are in retail stores all across California.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [