UPDATE companies SET description='Cherry Brook Woodworks operates from Canton, Connecticut, where in 2001 the Aleksa family purchased a home in the historic district and converted two antique apple barns into a woodworking shop.

The shop produces custom furniture, museum-quality antique reproductions, and repair and restoration services for heirloom pieces, all made by hand using traditional joinery and period-appropriate finishes. The workspace remains in the original barn structures on the family property, and the output ranges from one-off commissions to a rotating catalog of original designs such as Shaker tripod tables, sideboards, and chests crafted in tiger maple, birdseye maple, cherry, white oak, and walnut.

Clients include individual homeowners, interior designers, architects, and museums, with pieces shipped throughout the United States. The company has reproduced historic furniture from photographs or originals for institutional clients and restored family heirlooms for private owners.

Aleksa emphasizes a collaborative process, listening closely to each client to create furniture that fits specific spaces and styles, a level of personal involvement he contrasts with larger production shops. His approach stems from a belief that the relationship with the client is as important as the finished piece, and that honoring the materials and history behind each project results in furniture built to last generations.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Antique furniture reproduction", "Furniture repair and restoration", "Handcrafted furniture sales", "Period furniture making", "Custom woodworking"], "industries": ["Homeowners", "Interior designers", "Architects", "Museums"], "materials": ["Tiger Maple", "Birdseye Maple", "Cherry", "White Oak", "Walnut", "Oak"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Handmade custom furniture tailored to each client''s space and style", "Museum-quality antique reproductions from photos or originals", "Heirloom furniture repair and restoration", "Direct collaboration with the maker throughout the process", "Workshop housed in historic apple barns on the family property"], "facts_used": ["Location: Canton, Connecticut -> db", "Founded 2001 via family purchase of historic property and conversion of apple barns -> /about", "Founder Peter Aleksa, fine furniture maker with decades of experience -> /about", "Family-owned, wife and two boys involved -> /about", "Services: custom furniture, antique reproductions, repair/restoration, furniture for sale -> /about, /", "Processes: handmade, custom design, period furniture making, antique restoration -> /about, /", "Facility: two historic apple barns transformed into woodworking shop -> /about", "Industries served: homeowners, interior designers, architects, museums -> /about, /", "Materials: Tiger Maple, Birdseye Maple, Cherry, White Oak, Walnut, Oak -> / (product listings)", "Education: University of New Hampshire degree, specialized furniture making school, apprenticeship under master German furniture maker -> /about", "Differentiators: personal collaboration, customization, museum-quality replication, restoration as art -> /about, /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Peter Aleksa is a fine furniture maker with masterful skills who has spent decades making custom furniture and antique reproductions by hand for clients across the country.", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cherry-brook-woodworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Chicago Medical Engineering is based in Elmhurst, Illinois. Founded in 2019 by a team of engineers who recognized the importance of calibrated, high-performing medical imaging equipment, the company began as a response to a market gap for reliable pre-owned capital equipment and service.

The company supplies pre-owned medical imaging systems and parts—over 1,190 items across 16 equipment categories including CT scanners (362 systems), MRI scanners (77), cath/angio labs (63), portable X-ray (40), ultrasound transducers (32), and digital mammography units (23). It also provides service and maintenance for imaging and radiation therapy equipment: preventive maintenance, emergency repairs, calibration, compliance assurance, linear accelerator service, and part repair/exchange. A global network of engineers handles de‑installation, inspection, installation, and testing. The firm offers flexible warranty, leasing, and asset‑management options.

Customers include hospitals, outpatient diagnostic centers, radiation oncology clinics, and radiology departments worldwide. Testimonials cite a radiation oncology director, a VP of healthcare procurement, and a lead biomedical engineer. The company serves facilities needing turnkey clinical and diagnostic solutions, from equipment sourcing to installation and ongoing support.

