UPDATE companies SET description='Cinnamon Metals was founded in 2005 when a Manassas, Virginia roofing contractor, frustrated by weeks-long lead times for simple sheet metal orders, began fabricating parts in his home garage with the help of his wife, Cinnamon. The operation grew steadily and relocated to a dedicated shop in Springfield, Virginia in July 2014.

The company operates as a full-service custom metal fabricator, specializing in roofing, green roofing, and masonry products. Its capabilities include sheet metal fabrication, 3D product design, shop drawing and cut sheet creation, manufacturing consulting, and laser welding. Equipment includes a shear and computerized brake, a CNC turret punch (added 2019), a CNC press brake (added 2020), and laser welding capability (added 2021).

Cinnamon Metals serves commercial and residential roofing, masonry, and green roofing contractors, as well as landscaping and general construction firms. Its product lines cover commercial roofing panels, water control systems, masonry flashings, green roofing components, and custom fabrications.

The business was built on eliminating long wait times for contractors, emphasizing quick, reliable, and quality fabrication. It is an authorized fabricator manufacturing to ANSI/SPRI ES-1 standards and a member of the National Roofing Contractors Association (NRCA).', certifications=ARRAY['ANSI','ANSI/SPRI ES-1']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sheet metal fabrication for roofing", "Custom metal fabrication", "3D product design", "Shop drawing creation", "Cut sheet creation", "Manufacturing consulting", "Laser welding", "CNC turret punching", "CNC press brake forming", "Shear and computerized brake forming"], "industries": ["Roofing", "Green Roofing", "Masonry", "Landscaping", "Construction"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Shear & Computerized Brake", "CNC Turret Punch", "CNC Press Brake", "Laser Welding"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Quick, reliable, and quality fabrication with short lead times", "3D product design, shop drawings, and cut sheets for project approval", "Manufacturing consulting to optimize costs and time", "Authorized fabricator per ANSI/SPRI ES-1", "NRCA member"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2005 in Manassas garage by a roofing contractor and his wife Cinnamon -> /", "Relocated to Springfield, VA in July 2014 -> /", "Purchased CNC Turret Punch in January 2019 -> /", "Purchased CNC Press Brake in November 2020 -> /", "Added laser welding in February 2021 -> /", "Member of NRCA since October 2022 -> /", "Authorized fabricator per ANSI/SPRI ES-1 -> /", "Serves commercial and residential roofing, masonry, and green roofing contractors -> /", "Offers 3D product design, shop drawings, cut sheets, and manufacturing consulting -> /", "Equipment: shear & computerized brake, CNC turret punch, CNC press brake, laser welding -> /", "Headquarters: Springfield, Virginia -> db", "Certification: ANSI -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Cinnamon Metals is a full-service custom metal fabrication company specialized in roofing, green roofing, and masonry products.", "founded_year": "2005", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cinnamon-metals' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Circuit Breaker Source operates from Norco, California, and was founded in 2015. The company buys and sells new, used, obsolete, and surplus circuit breakers and related electrical equipment.

The business handles a range of breaker types including molded case, low-voltage, air, vacuum, insulated case, and panelboard models, along with transformers, panels, safety switches, motor control centers, and isolator switches. It also provides repair and testing, system upgrade and design, refurbishing to extend breaker life, supply and replacement, emergency response, and cleaning and lubrication services. Operations are nationwide; no facility size or headcount is disclosed.

Customers include electrical contractors with leftover project material, electrical distributors with slow-moving inventory, industrial facilities undergoing modernization, and construction companies with surplus stock. The company evaluates breakers by manufacturer, model, ratings, condition, quantity, and demand, and accepts single units or bulk lots.

