UPDATE companies SET description='Click Therapeutics is headquartered in New York, New York. Founded in 2012 by David Benshoof Klein, who recognized the impact of smartphones on behavior and cognition and began developing mobile-application-based treatments, coining the term "Digital Therapeutics™." The company is backed by biotech and pharma investors including HIG, Accelmed, and Sanofi Ventures.

The company develops, validates, and commercializes software as prescription medical treatments. Its multimodal platform, Click SE™, combines software with pharmacotherapy to create software-enhanced drug treatments. The team spans clinicians, researchers, and technologists who conduct clinical trials and manage regulatory submissions.

Click Therapeutics serves the life sciences, digital health, and medical device industries, working with pharmaceutical partners such as Otsuka to co-develop prescription digital therapeutics. Its treatments are prescribed by physicians and reimbursed as drug-software combination products, targeting patients with unmet needs in psychiatry, neurology, metabolic disease, and oncology.

The company was started to leverage software to improve clinical outcomes and bridge gaps in treatment access, aiming to provide patients everywhere access to safe and effective prescription digital therapeutics. Its differentiators include an AI-enabled platform, a first FDA-cleared prescription app for adjunctive MDD treatment developed with Otsuka, and a pipeline spanning multiple therapeutic areas.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Prescription digital therapeutic development", "Clinical trial design and execution", "FDA regulatory strategy and clearance", "Software platform development (Click SE\u2122)", "AI-enabled therapeutic design", "Neuromodulatory mechanism research", "Pharmaceutical co-development partnerships"], "industries": ["Life Sciences", "Digital Health", "Medical Devices", "Technology", "Artificial Intelligence"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Leading AI-enabled prescription digital therapeutics platform", "First and only FDA-cleared prescription app for adjunctive MDD treatment (developed with Otsuka)", "CT-132 met primary endpoint in pivotal trial for episodic migraine prevention", "Biotech/pharma investor base including HIG, Accelmed, Sanofi Ventures"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: New York, New York -> db", "Founding year: 2012 -> /about", "Founder: David Benshoof Klein -> /about", "Investors: HIG, Accelmed, Sanofi Ventures -> /about", "Certification: ISO 13485 -> db", "Platform: Click SE\u2122 (Software-Enhanced Drugs) -> /", "Products: CT-152 (Rejoyn), CT-155 (Motivista), AspyreRx, CT-132, and pipeline -> /about", "Collaboration with Otsuka for FDA-cleared MDD app -> /about", "Industries: life sciences, digital health, medical devices, technology, AI -> /about", "AI-enabled platform claim -> /about", "Clinical trial endpoints for CT-132 -> /about", "Awards: Builtin Best Places to Work, DHNY Hall of Fame 2025, Deloitte Technology Fast 5