UPDATE companies SET description='ClickFold Plastics was founded in 2001 in Charlotte, North Carolina, to address a gap in the market for custom plastic enclosures and parts in smaller volumes. The company operates from a facility on the North Carolina–South Carolina border near Charlotte Douglas International Airport, providing convenient logistics for domestic and cross-border shipments.

The company specializes in a zero-tooling fabrication process that produces custom plastic housings, enclosures, covers, panels, holders, spacers, lenses, bezels, guards, bumpers, and insulators without the need for injection molds. Core capabilities include CNC machining, 3D printing, digital graphics and UV printing, EMI shielding, assembly, packaging, custom kitting, and virtual prototyping. The process is geared toward low-volume production runs and just-in-time delivery, with a typical concept-to-production timeline of under four weeks.

ClickFold serves OEMs across industrial controls, medical devices, communications, gaming and simulators, building controls, measuring equipment, government and military, and commercial vehicles. Customers are typically companies that require custom plastic parts in smaller quantities delivered on a just-in-time basis, with support for rapid product development and prototyping.

The business was started to offer a cost-effective alternative to injection molding for low-volume needs and a more refined option than sheet metal forming. Its stated differentiators are the elimination of tooling costs, no minimum order quantities, fast turnaround, and ISO 9001 certification maintained since 2017.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Zero-tooling plastic fabrication", "CNC machining", "3D printing", "Digital graphics printing", "UV printing", "EMI shielding", "Assembly", "Packaging and kitting", "Virtual prototyping", "Rapid prototyping", "Metal substitution", "Reverse engineering", "CAD design and review", "Custom plastic enclosures", "Custom plastic parts"], "industries": ["Industrial Controls", "Medical Devices", "Communications", "Gaming/Simulators", "Building Controls", "Measuring Equipment", "Government/Military", "Commercial Vehicles"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Concept to production in under 4 weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Zero-tooling process eliminates need for expensive molds", "No minimum order quantities", "Concept to production in under 4 weeks", "Just-in-time delivery with 1\u20133 day ground shipping east of the Mississippi", "ISO 9001 certified since 2017"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2001 -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Charlotte, NC -> /about-us", "Zero-tooling fabrication process -> /about-us", "Capabilities: CNC machining, 3D printing, digital graphics, UV printing, EMI shielding, assembly, packaging -> /about-us", "Industries served: Industrial Controls, Medical Devices, Communications, Gaming/Simulators, Building Controls, Measuring Equipment, Government/Military, Commercial Vehicles -> /", "ISO 9001 certified since 2017 -> /about-us", "No minimum order quantities -> /", "Concept to production in under 4 weeks -> /", "Just-in-time delivery, 1-3 day ground shipping east of Mississippi -> /about-us", "Facility on NC/SC state line near Charlotte Douglas Airport -> /about-us", "Plastic materials US-manufactured, compliant with US/EU regulations -> /about-us", "Offers reverse engineering of injection molded parts or sheet metal housings -> /", "Provides virtual prototyping and CAD review process -> /about-us", "Serves OEMs requiring smaller volumes -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a leading manufacturer of custom plastic enclosures.", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "No minimum order quantity", "export_compliance": ["Exports to Canada and Mexico"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='clickfold-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Clore Automotive, LLC is based in Overland Park, Kansas. The company was founded in 2001, building on an over 50-year heritage in the automotive equipment aftermarket.

The company designs, develops, and manufactures a range of automotive service equipment, including jump starters, battery chargers, battery testers, maintainers, and work lights. Its product portfolio is organized under well-known brands such as Booster PAC, Jump-N-Carry, SOLAR, CHARGE IT!, Light-N-Carry, and PRO-LOGIX. Specific offerings include 12-volt portable jump starters, 100-amp flashing power supplies, 60/40/10-amp battery chargers, digital battery and system testers with integrated printers, and lithium jump starters. The company also provides technical support and repair services through its customer care and technical service teams.

Clore Automotive serves both professional technicians and consumers across the automotive aftermarket. Its equipment is used in professional service facilities and by individual vehicle owners. The company emphasizes meeting the evolving power needs of modern vehicles, with products optimized for a wide variety of battery types found in today''s vehicles.

The company differentiates itself through a focus on durability and longevity, stating that its products are built to exceed the rigorous demands of professional technicians and perform in tough environments long after competing products have failed. It also highlights superior customer care, with technical service teams that can diagnose problems, expedite parts, and refer customers to service centers. Continuous innovation in jump starter battery technology and a steady stream of new products addressing specific technician needs are cited as core drivers.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product design and development", "Manufacturing of automotive service equipment", "Technical support and repair service", "Battery testing and analysis", "Jump starter technology development"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Professional automotive service", "Consumer automotive"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Products engineered to exceed professional technician demands", "Technical service team with hands-on industry experience", "Continuous innovation in jump starter battery technology", "Broad product portfolio addressing specific technician needs", "Customer care accessible via phone, fax, and internet"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2001 with over 50-year heritage -> /about", "Headquarters in Overland Park, Kansas -> db", "Manufactures automotive service equipment under brands Booster PAC, Jump-N-Carry, SOLAR, CHARGE IT!, Light-N-Carry, PRO-LOGIX -> /about, /", "Serves professional technicians and consumers -> /about", "Offers technical support and repair service -> /about", "Focus on durability and longevity -> /about", "Continuous innovation in jump starter battery technology -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Clore Automotive is a leader in the design, development and manufacture of automotive service equipment for 