Wanderer at our Boutique Manufacturing Facility and Design Studio in Denver, Colorado.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='colorado-threads' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Columbus Machine Works operates from Columbus, Ohio, where it was founded in 1997 by Mike Stacey. Stacey, who holds a Bachelor of Science in Industrial Design, began as a job-shop machinist commuting by bicycle to serve local customers. His deep-rooted passion for machinery and manufacturing grew the business into a central Ohio hub for machining, metalwork, and craftsmanship.

The shop provides a full range of machining and fabrication services, including CNC milling (up to 84" x 32" x 30"), CNC turning (up to 20" diameter x 48" long), wire EDM, conventional machining, gear cutting, grinding, welding (TIG, MIG, stick, spray), and structural fabrication. Services also cover reverse engineering, on-site evaluation, inventory stocking, pickup and delivery, and 24/7 emergency breakdown response.

While the company serves a broad base of local manufacturers, its listed industry focus includes medical equipment. Customers range from small shops needing prototype parts to larger operations requiring OEM replacement components, jigs, fixtures, and repair of shafts, gears, and bearings.

